cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: >-
  From Lagging to Leading: The Measured Emergence of Standing Capacitance
  Behind Consumer Connections, 1997-2025 (extended version and
  reproducibility package)
authors:
  - family-names: Hume
    given-names: David
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-6920-0598"
version: 0.9.0
date-released: "2026-08-08"
repository-code: "https://github.com/djhume/lagging-to-leading"
abstract: >-
  Twenty-nine years of regulatory half-hourly metering at New Zealand grid
  exit points measure a national power system's reactive character crossing
  from lagging to leading overnight, attribute the drift dominantly to the
  demand side, and identify a standing distributed-capacitance term
  accumulating behind consumer connections at about 250 VAr per connection
  over 2013-2025, from a coefficient indistinguishable from zero until about
  2012. Includes the extended version of the paper and the full replication
  notebook suite computing every number from public data.
keywords:
  - reactive power
  - power factor
  - shunt capacitance
  - overvoltage
  - load modelling
  - power systems
notes: >-
  A condensed journal version is prepared for submission to the IEEE Open
  Access Journal of Power and Energy. DOI to be minted via Zenodo at public
  release.
